					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "ANCHOR POINT\n\nThe Anchor Point node can be use to extract a preset anchor point from a geometry node in order to set the origin on the Mesh2D node.\nIn short: it allows you to set from \"where\" the mesh is scaled, rotated and translated.\n\nIn this example we use the Anchor Point node to set the origin to the top left of the mesh.\nThis allows us to easily rotate around that point."
					}
				},
