					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "MESH2D\n\nThis tutorial will teach you how to use the Mesh2D type.\nWorking with meshes will introduce you to three other types: Transformation2D, Geometry2D and Camera2D. We will cover Transformation2D and Geometry2D in this tutorial and Camera2D in the next one.\n\nA 2D mesh is a geometrical surface on which a material is projected.\nMaterials can be colors or textures. \n\nMeshes are a very light type, meaning you can have hundreds of them before your GPU starts sweating."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 255.441802978515625,
					"width": 702.064453125,
					"x": -1260.4320068359375,
