					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "GEOMETRY\n\nGeometry is the starting point of your Mesh2D workflow.\nHere we have three geometry nodes, each of these nodes output Geometry2D as a type.\n\nAn important thing to remember is that geometry does not live in pixel space, but simply as a shape in a rectangular bounding box.\nThis can be seen when you select one of the nodes and take a look at the bottom of the monitor.\nInstead of a resolution you'll spot a min(n,n) and max(n,n,), this is the bounding box of the geometry.\nThis means that geometry is always resolution independent\n\nBesides having parameters to control the size of the geometry, we also have an inlet for UV.\nThe UV inlets want a Box2D type, we'll discuss UV's and Box2D in a separate tutorial."
					}
				},
