					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "TRANSFORMATION 2D\n\nTransformation2D is a type that contains X\/Y translation, width\/height and rotation data all in a single (normalized) type.\nThis permits you to use nodes like Grid Pattern (which is normalized), with meshes and cameras.\n\nIn this patch we're using the Grid Pattern and Linear node to create our transformation.\nAfter we convert it to a mesh2D we transform it again.\nNote that the Transformation2D affects all instances individually, but the transform after the Mesh2D node affects all meshes the same.\n\nAlso note that the float2 type will be converted to transformation2d in the Mesh2D node and will be used for X\/Y translation.\nAlso-Also note that color(float4)  and texture2d RGBA can be converted to material in the Mesh2D node."
					}
				},
