					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "MATERIAL & RENDERING\n\nTo translate geometry into a mesh we require the Mesh2D node.\nThis node will combine Geometry2d, Transform2d and Material into a Mesh2d type.\nNext, the Render2D node will render the mesh2D to a texture2D RGBA type.\n\nIn this example we start by creating a Rectangle geometry and make sure the width conforms to the aspect ratio of the patch.\nNext we take the Texture In (test card) and transform it into a material using the Texture Material node.\nBoth go into the Mesh2D node to create a Mesh2d type.\nAs you can see, the material is projected onto the rectangle.\nNext we render the mesh to a texture using the 2D Render"
					}
				},
